AT&T names Dorman chairman, succeeding Armstrong 
NEW YORK - AT&T Corp. said on Wednesday its president, David Dorman, will succeed C. Michael Armstrong as chairman and chief executive officer when the nation's largest telephone company sells its cable-television business to Comcast Corp.
Dorman's appointment, which was widely expected, will become effective once the sale of AT&T Broadband closes later this year.
